  "id": "DrugBank_DB09488 - MONDO_grouped_11786_5324_24332",
  "verbalization": "Acrivastine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis through a chain of indications that link it to Vasomotor Rhinitis, which in turn is associated with other drugs such as Isoflupredone Acetate, Mizolastine, and Ramatroban. These drugs are all indicated for Vasomotor Rhinitis, a condition characterized by inflammation of the nasal mucosa due to vascular responses, often triggered by environmental factors. The shared indication for Vasomotor Rhinitis across these drugs suggests a common mechanism of action, possibly involving the modulation of vascular tone or inflammatory mediators. The evidence from the three paths, which all show Acrivastine as a precursor to Vasomotor Rhinitis, and then to Allergic Rhinitis, supports a potential role for Acrivastine in the treatment or management of allergic rhinitis through this indirect pathway. The integration of these paths highlights a recurring mechanism of vascular and inflammatory regulation, which may explain the observed relationships.",
